--[[
disable-input-rotation-map - stop KOReader from remapping physical keys on rotation.

Replaces Device.input.rotation_map with empty tables for all four rotations.
That map is read in one place (input.lua:813) and renames key events to follow
the screen: Up -> Right, LPgBack -> LPgFwd and so on. Emptying it makes the
physical keys keep their unrotated names, which is what devices whose firmware
already reports keys by gravity need.

Ships DISABLED (`.lua.disabled`): KOReader 2026.07.1 already calls
Input:disableRotationMap() itself for the Onyx models that need it -- go7,
gocolor7, gocolor7_2, hibreak, moaanmix7, xiaomi_reader (koreader#12423) --
which installs exactly this same empty map, so the patch is redundant there.
Rename to `2-disable-input-rotation-map.lua` and restart KOReader only on a
device that needs it and is not on that list.

Targets:
  - KOReader 2026.07.1 (safe_version 202607010000)
  - KOReader core (device input layer)
--]]

local Device = require("device")
Device.input.rotation_map = {[0]={}, [1]={}, [2]={}, [3]={}}